  "bodyText": "Skip to content S ORGANIZATION Science Students Academy Search… K Dashboard Calendar Lessons Courses PEOPLE Students Clients Tutors Team LIBRARY Recordings Resources TO REVIEW Report approvals Safeguarding Unlinked sessions ORGANIZATION Settings EU Emmanuel Usang Admin · Science Students Academy Help and updates New updates available You're currently on a free trial. Set up billing to continue using Bobbin. Set up billing Atlas Research Course Actions New lesson Summary Course outline Lessons (1) Resources Homework Back to plan MODULE 1 OF 9 Algebraic Notation and Manipulation Build fluency with algebraic language, expressions, substitution and equivalent forms. Edit module WHY THIS ORDER Establishes the symbolic fluency needed for every later algebra topic. Weekly practice: short simplification and substitution sets. Retrieval check: notation and integer arithmetic quiz. Formative milestone: explain and correct errors in a mixed manipulation task. Notation and substitution Interpret algebraic notation and evaluate expressions by substituting values. 0 of 2 Translate between verbal statements and algebraic expressions, including multiplication, powers and brackets. Mark covered Substitute positive and negative integers into expressions and calculate accurately. Mark covered Simplifying and expanding Collect terms and use the distributive law to transform expressions. 0 of 2 Simplify expressions by collecting like terms, including terms with powers. Mark covered Expand a single bracket and simplify the resulting expression. Mark covered Factorising and formulae Reverse expansion and rearrange formulae in simple contexts. 0 of 2 Factorise expressions by taking out a common factor. Mark covered Change the subject of a one-step or two-step formula. Mark covered Linear Equations and Inequalities",
